{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":23606,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"0f2c217888c87b221458180667353038fc366d1eac296df2db61a4c7c51555e4","packTokens":8883,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":8606,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nState, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall provide email-and-password sign-in, send the submitted credentials to the sign-in service, display the resulting landing page or authentication error, render navigation and actions according to the signed-in user's returned permissions, and clear authenticated page data and return to sign-in when an authenticated session expires or a protected request returns HTTP 401.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The sign-in screen is displayed and the authentication service accepts the submitted credentials and returns the user and permissions when The user submits an email address and password then The screen shows the returned operational landing page and navigation actions allowed by the returned permissions\",\n    \"Given The sign-in screen is displayed and the authentication service refuses the submitted credentials when The user submits an email address and password then The screen shows the returned error message and remains on the sign-in page\",\n    \"Given An authenticated screen displays protected data and the session expires or a protected request receives HTTP 401 when The web app handles the expired session or 401 response then The screen returns to sign-in and no protected page data remains displayed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"Where mock procurement and receiving import is available, the feedlot web app shall let operationally authorized users preview and submit selected records through the documented mock-data adapter and display the returned import result and source fields.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An operationally authorized user opens the import screen and mock adapter records are available when The user previews the source records then The screen displays each available record's vendor, source identifier, cost, head count, animal weight, breed, age, source, purchase-order, and receiving fields\",\n    \"Given An operationally authorized user has selected mock source records when The user submits the import then The import request contains the selected source records and the screen displays the response status, imported-record list, and returned created or updated counts when supplied\",\n    \"Given A user without operational access opens the import screen when The screen renders using the user's returned permissions then The screen displays imported records and does not show an enabled import action\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let operationally authorized users map PO lines to one or more lots and lots to one or more pens, retain allocated animal quantities, and display the resulting traceability and pen information.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An imported PO line is allocated across multiple lots and a lot is allocated across multiple pens when The mapping screen renders the returned mappings then The screen shows each PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen relationship with its allocated animal quantity\",\n    \"Given A mapping response contains pen information when The mapping screen renders the response then The screen displays each mapped pen's ID, capacity, current animal count, and mapped allocation quantity\",\n    \"Given An operationally authorized user changes mapping quantities, or a user without operational access opens the mapping screen when The authorized user saves mappings or the other user's screen renders using returned permissions then The screen displays the saved mapping values returned by the service, and for a user without operational access it displays existing mappings without mapping-change actions\",\n    \"Given An edited allocation conflicts with a PO line's returned head count or a pen's returned capacity and the mapping service refuses the save when The user submits the mapping changes then The screen displays the returned error and the last saved mapping values remain displayed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an operational user repeats an import containing previously imported source-system identifiers, the feedlot web app shall display the import result for the matched records returned by the import service without presenting them as newly created duplicates, and flag returned allocation conflicts when an updated head count is below existing mapped quantities.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The import response identifies source records as matched to existing records when The repeated import completes then The screen displays the matched record list and response status without displaying those records as newly created duplicates\",\n    \"Given A repeated-import response updates a PO line's head count below its existing mapped allocation quantities and returns an allocation conflict when The repeated import completes then The screen displays the matched record, returned head count, existing mapped quantities, and an allocation-conflict flag without presenting the record as a new duplicate\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall display market-date and target-weight forecasts from incoming animal data and configured yard defaults, use lot-specific overrides when present, show a forecast as unavailable without a positive gain rate, and expose forecast-assumption editing only to authorized managers.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The forecast response contains incoming animal data, yard defaults, and a lot-specific override when A user opens the lot forecast then The screen displays the returned incoming data, target weight, expected gain rate, projected market date, and forecast basis using the lot-specific override\",\n    \"Given A lot forecast has no positive gain rate available when The user opens the forecast then The projected date field displays an unavailable value on the screen\",\n    \"Given An authorized manager changes a yard default or lot-specific override, or a user without manager authorization opens forecast settings when The manager saves the assumption or the other user's screen renders then The screen displays the returned forecast values for saved changes, and does not show assumption-edit actions to a user without manager authorization\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall display feed inventory items and stock movements and let authorized inventory users maintain items, record receipts or adjustments, and change wastage settings, while displaying inventory details to users with viewing access.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The inventory response contains feed items and stock movements when A user opens the inventory screen then The screen displays each item's name, category, available quantity, unit, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, storage location, wastage setting when returned, and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values\",\n    \"Given An authorized inventory user records a receipt or adjustment, edits an item, or changes wastage settings when The user submits the change then The screen displays the saved inventory record and stock-movement values returned by the service\",\n    \"Given A user has inventory viewing access but lacks inventory-edit access when The user opens inventory then The screen displays inventory values and does not show enabled item, receipt, adjustment, or wastage-edit actions\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall display inventory projections for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semi-annual, and annual horizons using saved upcoming feed plans and configured wastage, while presenting known actual wastage separately from delivered-feed consumption.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The projection response contains available stock, upcoming saved feed plans, and wastage-adjusted estimates when A user selects each supported projection horizon then The screen displays the returned projected consumption and closing or remaining inventory for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semi-annual, and annual horizons, along with the configured wastage ratio\",\n    \"Given The projection response has no saved upcoming feed plans for an item when A user opens inventory projections then The screen displays the response's empty-data state for that item's projected inventory\",\n    \"Given The inventory service returns a known actual-wastage movement and delivered-feed consumption when A user views the stock movement list then The screen lists actual wastage as a separate movement from delivered-feed consumption\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let authorized ration managers create, revise, optimize, and approve ration definitions, display ingredient proportions, nutrition and cost values, and present the lowest-cost candidate mix meeting user-selected nutritional requirements without saving it until the user chooses to do so.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authorized ration manager creates or revises a ration when The manager enters ration details and ingredient proportions then The screen displays fields for ration name and type, ingredients, proportions, intended animal type or weight range, dry matter, energy, and cost per unit\",\n    \"Given The ration service returns nutrition values and calculated ingredient-mix cost when The ration screen renders the response then The screen displays the returned nutrition values and calculated cost per pound\",\n    \"Given An authorized ration manager has selected nutrition requirements and candidate mixes when The manager runs optimization then The screen identifies the returned lowest-cost mix that meets the selected requirements and displays its nutrition and cost values with a separate save action\",\n    \"Given An optimized candidate is displayed and the user has not selected a save action, or a user without ration-management access opens the ration screen when The screen renders then The candidate is displayed without being shown as a saved ration, and the unauthorized user's screen displays existing rations without create, revise, optimize, or approve actions\",\n    \"Given The optimization response indicates that no candidate mix meets the selected nutrition requirements when The manager views the optimization result then The screen displays that no mix qualifies and does not show an enabled save action for a qualifying mix\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let authorized planners generate or adjust dated pen-level feed plans from bunk rates, ration assignments, and animal counts, and display the returned plan details and execution status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authorized planner selects a date, pen, bunk rate, ration, and animal count when The planner submits the plan then The plan request contains those selected values and the screen displays the returned plan's date, pen, assigned lot or lots, animal count, ration, planned quantity, planned time, quantity per animal, total feed cost, expected energy intake, and status\",\n    \"Given A user lacks planning access and opens feed planning when The screen renders using the user's returned permissions then The screen displays existing plans without plan-generation or plan-adjustment actions\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall flag a saved plan for review when relevant inputs change, retain its saved values until an authorized planner confirms an update or regenerates it, allow assigned-pen operators to update execution status while withholding enabled status-update actions from other operators and displaying returned refusals for rejected updates, and show intake variance without automatically rewriting the saved plan.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A saved plan's pen count, bunk rate, animal count, or ration assignment changes after generation when The user opens the plan then The screen displays the saved plan unchanged and a review flag\",\n    \"Given An authorized planner opens a plan flagged for review when The plan screen renders then The screen shows authorized confirm-update and regenerate actions\",\n    \"Given An authorized planner confirms an update or regenerates a flagged plan when The planner submits the selected action then The plan request contains the selected action and the screen displays the response status and returned plan\",\n    \"Given An operator is assigned to the plan's pen when The operator updates the execution status then The screen displays the returned status value for that pen's plan\",\n    \"Given Actual bunk intake differs from the saved plan when The user views the feeding plan and activity then The screen displays actual intake and variance while the saved plan values remain unchanged\",\n    \"Given An operator is not assigned to the plan's pen and the screen renders using the operator's returned permissions when The operator opens the plan then The screen displays the current status and does not show an enabled status-update action\",\n    \"Given The service refuses a status update submitted by an operator who is not assigned to the plan's pen when The operator submits the status update then The screen displays the returned refusal error and the current plan status remains displayed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let operational users record feeding activity by pen and lot, including per-lot allocations when a pen contains multiple lots, display the returned variance, cost, energy, inventory consumption, feeding status, and lot-level consumption and cost totals, display a returned stock error when insufficient stock prevents saving, provide permission-controlled correction and void actions for saved feeding events, and display a timed-out save outcome as unknown while leaving retry resolution to the existing service/user workflow.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An operational user enters feeding date, pen, ration, planned quantity, actual delivered quantity, and status for a pen containing one or more lots when The user submits the feeding event then The feeding request contains the entered fields and a delivered-quantity allocation for each affected lot, and the screen displays the response status and returned event fields including the lot allocations\",\n    \"Given A successful feeding response contains calculated values when The event screen renders the response then The screen displays actual-minus-planned variance, feed cost, energy value, inventory consumed by ingredient, and cumulative lot feed consumption and cost\",\n    \"Given A successful feeding response contains planned quantity of 100 pounds, actual delivered quantity of 115 pounds, and a returned variance value of 15 pounds when The event screen renders the response then The screen displays the returned variance value of 15 pounds\",\n    \"Given A feeding response includes actual delivered quantity and an inventory movement when The event screen renders the response then The screen displays stock consumption for the delivered quantity and known wastage as a separate movement rather than added delivered feed\",\n    \"Given The service refuses a feeding event because available stock is insufficient when The user submits the event then The screen displays the returned stock error and does not display the event as saved\",\n    \"Given A user without operational access opens feeding activity when The screen renders then The screen displays existing activity without an action to record a feeding event\",\n    \"Given A feeding-event save request times out without a definitive response when The web app handles the timeout then The screen displays that the save outcome is unknown and retains the submitted event fields\",\n    \"Given A user has returned permission to correct or void saved feeding events when The user opens a saved feeding event then The screen shows correction and void actions\",\n    \"Given A user lacks returned permission to correct or void saved feeding events when The user opens a saved feeding event then The screen displays the event without enabled correction or void actions\",\n    \"Given An authorized user submits a correction and the service returns the corrected event with updated inventory movement and lot totals when The correction response is displayed then The screen displays the returned corrected event, inventory movement, and lot consumption and cost totals\",\n    \"Given An authorized user submits a void and the service returns the voided event with updated inventory movement and lot totals when The void response is displayed then The screen displays the returned void status, inventory movement, and lot consumption and cost totals\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let authorized livestock or operations users add lot weight measurements and display each lot's measurement history as a time-ordered series with returned measurement and gain information.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authorized user enters a lot weight measurement when The user submits the measurement then The measurement request contains lot, date, animals weighed, average animal weight, total lot weight when entered, and notes, and the screen displays the response status and saved measurement\",\n    \"Given The weight response contains multiple measurements when A user views the lot's weight history then The screen displays returned measurements in date order with weight gain since the previous measurement where returned\",\n    \"Given A user without measurement-entry access opens a lot's weight history when The screen renders then The screen displays the measurement time series without an enabled add-measurement action\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall display returned lot feed-to-gain metrics for days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed in pounds, feed conversion ratio, cost of gain, and projected ship date, and refresh displayed metrics after feeding or weight records change.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The lot metrics response contains receiving date, entry and current average weight, feed totals, feed cost, target weight, ADG, and projected ship date when A user opens lot performance then The screen displays the returned days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed in pounds, feed conversion ratio, cost of gain, and projected ship date\",\n    \"Given A lot has no positive ADG available when The user opens the lot performance screen then The screen displays the projected ship date as unavailable\",\n    \"Given A feeding or weight record is saved and the service returns updated lot metrics when The user opens or refreshes lot performance after the save then The screen displays the recalculated metric values returned for the updated records\",\n    \"Given The lot metrics response contains days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed, feed conversion ratio, cost of gain, and projected ship date for a lot with multiple animals when A user opens lot performance then The screen displays each metric value returned by the service without substituting a web-calculated value\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall present explainable rule-based suggestions for feeding adjustments or sale timing based on lot weight-gain trends and leave any resulting plan or sale change to an authorized planner's explicit action.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The insights service returns a feeding-adjustment or sale-timing suggestion and its supporting trend data or rule when The user opens lot insights then The screen displays the suggestion and its returned explanation or cited basis\",\n    \"Given A suggestion is displayed and the user has not chosen an action when The user views the suggestion then The screen displays the saved feed plan unchanged and does not change the sale date\",\n    \"Given An authorized planner chooses to act on a displayed suggestion when The planner submits the corresponding change then The change request contains the planner's selected action and the screen displays the response status\",\n    \"Given A user without planning access views a suggestion or the service refuses that user's attempted plan change when The user opens lot insights or submits the change request then The screen does not show an enabled plan-change action, or displays the returned refusal error, and the saved feed plan remains unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall display a dashboard of yard and lot performance, inventory, feeding, weight, cost, and energy values and let users select the measure used to rank best- and worst-performing lots.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The dashboard service returns yard, lot, pen, inventory, ration, feeding, weight, and performance values when A user opens the dashboard then The screen displays active lot and pen counts, animals per lot and pen, inventory status, ration usage, daily bunk rate per pen, planned versus actual feed, total feed consumed and cost, starting and current weight, total gain, ADG, feed-to-gain ratio, cost per unit of gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots\",\n    \"Given The dashboard displays best- and worst-performing lot rankings when The user selects FCR, ADG, or cost of gain as the ranking measure then The screen shows the lot ranking and selected measure as its basis\",\n    \"Given The dashboard response contains no value for a summary field when A user opens the dashboard then The screen displays the returned empty-data state for that field\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall provide filterable operational reports for inventory, feeding, lot performance, and profitability that answer the requested pen, lot, ration, plan-variance, inventory, and cost-of-gain questions and export the filtered results as CSV.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The operational report service returns records for multiple pens, lots, rations, feed plans, inventory items, and feed costs when A user opens the reports screen and applies its available filters then The screen shows which pen consumed the most feed, which lot has the best FCR and highest ADG, which ration is used most, planned-versus-actual feed and over- or under-feeding pens, remaining inventory, and feed cost per unit of weight gain\",\n    \"Given A filtered operational report is displayed when The user exports the report as CSV then The downloaded file contains the filtered report rows shown on the screen\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall display dashboards, reports, and exports using only records and profitability fields returned for the signed-in user's authorized yards and permissions, and remove previously displayed data from view and subsequent exports when returned permissions change.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The service response contains only records for the user's authorized yards and profitability fields allowed by the user's returned permissions when The user opens a dashboard or report then The screen shows only the returned authorized-yard records and permitted profitability fields\",\n    \"Given A user exports a filtered dashboard or report view when The export is generated then The downloaded file contains only the authorized-yard records and profitability fields shown to that user\",\n    \"Given A dashboard or report displays records or profitability fields and an updated permissions response removes access to some of that data when The web app processes the updated permissions then The screen no longer displays the records or fields no longer permitted, and a subsequent downloaded file contains only currently permitted records and fields\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall provide a feed-to-gain report comparing lot ADG, FCR, and cost of gain, with date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters, and CSV or PDF exports of filtered results subject to the user's returned permissions.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The report service returns lot records with weight and feeding data for a selected date range when The user selects date-range, breed, sex, or pen filters then The report request contains the selected filters and the screen displays matching lots with ADG, FCR, and cost-of-gain values calculated from records in the selected date range\",\n    \"Given Records without sex data are included in the report result set when The user views the sex filter then The screen displays the sex filter as unavailable for records without sex data\",\n    \"Given The user has applied report filters and has export access when The user exports the report as CSV or PDF then The downloaded file contains the filtered report rows shown on the screen and omits any yard or profitability fields not permitted by returned permissions\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall provide a filterable on-screen lot profitability list for authorized yards and display a CSV file containing the filtered authorized results when the user exports the list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The service returns profitability rows for yards authorized to the user when The user opens and filters the lot profitability view then The screen displays only the returned authorized-yard rows and their available profitability values\",\n    \"Given The user has applied filters to the authorized lot profitability list when The user selects CSV export then The downloaded file contains the filtered authorized rows displayed by the screen\",\n    \"Given The service indicates that the user cannot view profitability values when The user opens the lot profitability view then The screen hides profitability values\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall let an authorized user load visibly distinct sample data, prevent duplicate sample loading while displaying the returned result, require confirmation before sample-data reset or replacement, distinguish sample records from operational records, exclude sample records from operational report and inventory-total views and their exports, and display dashboard and yard-summary aggregate values as returned by the service.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Sample data is available and has not been loaded when An authorized user loads the sample data then The screen shows the returned sample records with a visible sample-data designation distinguishing them from operational records\",\n    \"Given Sample data is already loaded or a duplicate load is refused when A user attempts to load sample data then The screen displays the returned duplicate-load result and the returned record list contains no duplicate sample records\",\n    \"Given A user starts a sample-data reset or replacement but has not confirmed when The confirmation dialog is displayed and the user cancels then The screen shows the existing sample records unchanged and the reset or replacement request is not sent\",\n    \"Given A user confirms a sample-data reset or replacement when The service returns the operation result then The screen displays the returned operation status and resulting sample-data list or record count when supplied\",\n    \"Given A user lacks sample-data management permission and opens the sample-data controls when The screen renders using the user's returned permissions then The screen displays sample records and does not show enabled load, reset, or replacement actions\",\n    \"Given The service refuses a sample-data load, reset, or replacement because the user lacks permission when The user submits the operation then The screen displays the returned error and the existing sample-data list remains displayed\",\n    \"Given The service response contains sample and operational records for operational reports or inventory totals when A user opens one of those operational views then The screen displays report or inventory values based only on operational records and labels any sample records shown as sample data\",\n    \"Given A user exports an operational report or inventory view when the service response contains sample and operational records when The user generates the export then The downloaded file contains operational records only and excludes sample records\",\n    \"Given The dashboard or yard-summary response contains aggregate values, including values that may reflect sample and operational records when A user opens the dashboard or yard summary then The screen displays the returned aggregate values as provided without excluding or recalculating values that may include sample records\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall display a yard-level summary of active-lot total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost using returned aggregate values, and show unavailable values when required source data is missing.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The summary service returns active-lot aggregate values when A user with yard-summary access opens the yard summary then The screen displays total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost for the returned active lots\",\n    \"Given The summary service returns no data for one or more summary metrics when A user opens the yard summary then The screen displays returned available values and an explicit unavailable value for each missing field\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The feedlot web app shall provide a delivery overview or presentation page containing the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demo entry point, prompts used, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The delivery overview or presentation page is available when A user opens the page then The screen displays sections or links for the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demo entry point, prompts used, testing and validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market analysis\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"Every page shall render responsively at phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\",\n  \"Every web page shall remain usable at phone, tablet, and desktop widths without horizontal page scrolling, and touch controls at the narrow viewport shall have a minimum target size of 44 by 44 CSS pixels.\",\n  \"Every web-app page shall render without horizontal page overflow at phone, tablet, and desktop reference widths.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}